<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37656" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-gusto</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To taste beforehand</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 4, 33</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 3, 9, § 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pocula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					6, 633</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potum regis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					12, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caro bestiis praegustata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 22, 31</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>to take</i>, <i>eat</i>, or <i>drink beforehand</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicamina, for antidota,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					6, 660</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
